flowchart TB
  accTitle: Separate action authority and interruption control
  accDescr: The model proposes an action and supplies evidence and uncertainty, but a policy authority evaluates the exact action, scope, reversibility, and required approval. Separately, a monitor may request preemption or interruption, followed by a safe-boundary checkpoint and explicit cancellation reconciliation.
  P[Model action proposal] --> E[Evidence and uncertainty lineage]
  P --> G[Policy authorization gate]
  E --> G
  G -->|authorized within scope| X[Execute through tool contract]
  G -->|approval or refusal| H[Human decision or safe refusal]
  X --> M[Execution monitor]
  M -->|continue| X
  M -->|preempt or interrupt| S[Safe-boundary request]
  S --> C[Checkpoint and side-effect reconciliation]
  C --> R[Suspend or resume validation]
